[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise.
Read by what each report describes, #4471 holds two problems. The fix queued for the parser closes
one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket and its own count.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## The problems

### `swap`: day and month trade places

Every tenant in #4471 writes the day first. Their dates come out month first: 7 April becomes
4 July. This is the problem #4471 was opened for, and the queued parser fix is for this one.

The old table splits off a `hint` cause: tenants on `booking-v3` whose reports came through the
form. Those reports describe the same swap, in the same words, and nothing in them tells the two
apart. One problem, one ticket. If the parser fix leaves `booking-v3` form bookings swapped, that is
the time to open a ticket for the form.

<ProblemReports ticket={4471} problem="swap" />

### `day-move`: one day off, not a month

These reports describe no swap. A booking moves by one day, an invite arrives before the booking
was made, two clients in different time zones get different days for the same meeting, every June
booking is off by a day. That is a time zone or day boundary problem, not date order. The desk
already noted them (`desk-notes.json`), and the old table still counts them under `parser`. The
parser fix will not close them.

<ProblemReports ticket={4471} problem="day-move" />

## Why one ticket hid two

Reports are merged on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
Subjects like "Date is wrong" fit both problems, so all of them landed in #4471. The old table, for
comparison: it splits the swap in two by way in, and footnotes the one-day moves.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- Before you mark a big ticket known, read what its reports describe, not only their subjects.
- A report that does not fit the cause gets its own ticket, not a footnote.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
